    "body": "claim released: Codex (len) · 2026-11-27 · STOPPED: the failure does not reproduce here, so no pinning test can start red.\n\nWhat the CI log shows:\n- Run 46027502982 gives no panic text for `example_catalog`. It shows only `FAIL in 138s` and libtest's `slow (>60s)` notes for `catalog_3d_rough_finish::rebuilds` and `catalog_3d_rough_finish::regenerates`.\n- This agrees with the 60 s budget in `crates/app/tests/example_catalog/support.rs` (`within`). It is the known load failure of #3975.\n\nWhat I tried on `upstream/main` 751a79b20 (32 cores, debug):\n- The two cases alone, `--test-threads=2`, idle: 25.1 s and 25.5 s.\n- The same two cases while two other runs of the full `example_catalog` suite ran (`--include-ignored --test-threads=32`): 30.4 s and 32.4 s.\n- The two load runs: rough-finish 32.7-34.6 s, adaptive-pocket 30.2-35.9 s. All passed.\n- A 96-loop CPU load script and `taskset -c 0` needed approval. I did not run them.\n\nRecommended fix (not done): move the two cases to the app heavy lane, the same as #3163 did for `2d/adaptive-pocket` (`#[ignore = \"heavy lane (#3975 3d/rough-finish): ...\"]`). The other five tests of `catalog_3d_rough_finish` read the committed `.nc` and stay in quick. #3975 says that the maintainer selects the fix. This issue also closes itself on the next green post-merge run.\n\nNo branch was pushed. The local branch was empty and is deleted.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
